          "id": "6dd7c777eb2768f40c2ab8c7816856a795072e26",
          "message": "fix(site): /app hard-navigates to the overlaid hosted GUI, not a broken soft-nav .txt (sq-vw3ax.11) [OPUS-4.8] (#1352)\n\n* fix(site): /app hard-navigates to the overlaid hosted GUI, not a broken soft-nav .txt (sq-vw3ax.11) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe reported bug — /app \"serves a .txt instead of a real page\" — is a CROSS-APP\nsoft-navigation bug, not a stale export. VERIFY-FIRST corrected two premises in the\ndesign spec against the live repo:\n\n  * `site/out` is gitignored (site/.gitignore:/out) and built FRESH every deploy by\n    pages.yml — there is no committed export to drift. No export-parity CI check is\n    needed (it would be dead machinery over a non-committed tree).\n  * The hosted web GUI HAS shipped: gui/app is a real, actively-developed workbench\n    (recent sq-tp1m / sq-xvj9 features) that pages.yml (sq-vnd0i, maintainer's Option B)\n    builds with build:web and OVERLAYS at /sparq/app/, deliberately replacing the site\n    placeholder. e2e/site-nav.spec.ts hard-asserts the \"App\" slot + /gui->/app.\n\nRoot cause: the site linked to /app via next/link (soft nav) and /gui redirected via\nrouter.replace (soft nav), but /app is a SEPARATE Next.js app. A soft nav across two\ndistinct Next builds fetches the foreign RSC Flight payload /sparq/app/index.txt and\nrenders a raw .txt. Fix = make navigation to /app a HARD, full-page load:\n\n  * app-shell NavLink: an `external` nav item renders a plain <a href={withBasePath(/app/)}>\n    (Next does not auto-prefix a hand-written anchor; trailing slash matches trailingSlash).\n  * redirect-stub: a `hard` redirect uses window.location.assign(withBasePath(/app/));\n    the /surface/* + /about stubs keep the soft router.replace (same-site).\n  * /gui page: passes `hard`.\n  * /app placeholder: kept (the lychee link-target before the overlay, the site-only /\n    next dev / e2e destination, and a fallback) but its copy is corrected — it no longer\n    falsely says \"coming soon / being built\" (the hosted GUI is live at /sparq/app), and\n    the CTAs are re-weighted (primary \"Use it now, in this tab -> /try\").\n\nDELIBERATE DEVIATION from the design spec (documented per proceed-and-document): the spec\nasked to REMOVE the \"App\" top-bar slot until the hosted GUI ships. It has shipped and is\ndeployed at /sparq/app (maintainer's explicit Option B, sq-vnd0i); removing the slot would\nregress a live feature and break e2e. The slot is kept; the navigation mechanism is fixed.\n\nGates: cd site && npm run build (static export, /app + /app/index.txt emitted) OK; npm run\nlint clean; tsc --noEmit clean; e2e site-nav.spec.ts + redirect-stubs.spec.ts 20/20 pass.\nWASM prereq: js `npm run build:wasm` built (artifact only, no crates/ source change).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(site): use window.location.replace for hard redirects to keep stub out of back-stack [OPUS-4.8]\n\nassign() adds a history entry; replace() does not — matches the stated \"keep the dead route\nout of history\" intent in the component header comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
