          "distinct": true,
          "id": "63b8b2f011d02f29945ec3928790ae11a56d504c",
          "message": "docs(governance): tier-1 embedding-API stability + deprecation policy + in-code markers (sq-tvuw8) [OPUS-4.8] (#1372)\n\n* docs(governance): tier-1 embedding-API stability + deprecation policy + in-code markers (sq-tvuw8) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nAdds docs/api-stability.md — the doc-of-record proposing the tier-1\n(proposed-stable) public API surface (the sparq_serve::embed in-process\ndata-path facade + generation-ring concurrency wrapper, and the sparq-solid\nPodStore per-resource WAC-decision surface) plus the semver + deprecation-window\nguarantees a future stable line would carry. Everything else is tier-2/experimental.\n\nGrounds #1346's P0 consumer requirement (solid-server-rs git-pins an unstable\nembedded API today) and tees up the maintainer's semver-tier-1 freeze ratification\n(#1248 items 1+2). The freeze is NOT declared active here — that is @jeswr's\ngovernance call; this is the proposal + the in-code annotation.\n\nMarks the proposed tier-1 surface in-code with lightweight, non-breaking rustdoc\nmarkers (module-level on the embed facade + decide module; item-level on the\nPodStore decision fns and WacDecision) that link back to the policy doc. Syncs the\nsparq-serve/sparq-solid READMEs and the http-server/access-control SKILLs.\n\nNo behaviour change, no API change. Rustdoc (default + all-features, -D warnings)\nclean; doctests + clippy green in both feature states; readme-template + privacy-\nclaims gates pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(docs): replace em-dash in Status heading anchor (lychee offline gate)\n\nThe `## Status — PROPOSED, not yet in force` heading produced anchor\n`#status--proposed-not-yet-in-force` via the em-dash + surrounding spaces;\nlychee v0.23.0 (the action-pinned version) on x86_64 CI treats the resulting\ndouble-hyphen as ambiguous and fails to resolve it. Replace `—` with `:` so\nthe anchor becomes the unambiguous `#status-proposed-not-yet-in-force` and\nupdate the three in-file references accordingly. Doc-only; no .rs changes.\n\n[OPUS-4.8]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(docs): join deprecate-then-remove bold phrase onto one line (rendering nit) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nSoft-wrap inside `**...**` rendered as \"deprecate-then- remove\" (with an\nunwanted space after the hyphen). Join onto a single line — no semantic change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
